  "notes": "Clean lane: no new quantified, reproducible exploit in the go-core chunk beyond the known ledger (policy base_ref/lifetime/rename/whitespace bypasses in internal/acdsl/policy.go and git.go are already carried there and were not re-reported). Scope: all 34 manifest files read in full; nothing excluded. Examined and rejected: ExpandInstallMarkers (install.env is local, installer-written, same trust domain as the repo); startPeek /healthz identity check (a co-resident user could spoof a matching identity, but the pre-change code reused any listener unconditionally and peek's loopback ports are unauthenticated to every local user anyway, so no new boundary is crossed); folderDialogScript PowerShell %q interpolation (only constant prompts reach it, internal/server/config_items.go:45 and repos.go:635); evals nested skillRoot join (skill.Name comes from the enumerated skill list, artifact route matches d/f against loader output, internal/server/skill_tests.go); sessions validateScopeName blocks '', '.', '..', separators and the archive container; RunSync logs only basename/duration. Cross-chunk suspicions for the station: (1) the policy gate's promise in cmd/acdsl/main.go:13-14 ('strict/gated repos may not change rules or verifiers off the base branch') covers only acdsl/policy.json, policy.schema.json, registry.json, evalgen.json and declaration lines; verifier implementations (cmd/acdsl/verifiers/** sources run via go run, prebuilt bin/verifiers/<pkg> picked up by resolveVerifierBinary in internal/acdsl/registry.go:65-80, and shipped bin/verifiers/* in dist targets) are outside policySurface, so a branch that edits or drops a verifier binary changes rule outcomes with zero policy diagnostics. Not filed as a finding because the runner itself (./bin/acdsl, Makefile:46) sits in the same agent-writable tree, so whether this is a boundary crossing depends on the trust model enforced by cmd/hooks/acdsl-policy-guard.sh, which is outside this chunk. (2) ArchiveScope/